---
import "../../styles/global.css";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import CallToAction from "../../components/CallToAction.astro";
import PredirectDemo from "../../components/PredirectDemo.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Case Study — Predirect"
  description="How Predirect went from a personal itch to a 270★ privacy extension that rewrites 30+ tracked sites to privacy-friendly frontends."
>
  <Header />

  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 px-4">
    <div
      class="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-white border-3 border-black p-8 sm:p-12 relative shadow-[6px_6px_0_#000]"
    >
      <div class="size-2 bg-white border-2 border-black absolute -top-2 -right-2"></div>
      <div class="size-2 bg-white border-2 border-black absolute -top-2 -left-2"></div>
      <div class="size-2 bg-white border-2 border-black absolute -bottom-2 -left-2"></div>
      <div class="size-2 bg-white border-2 border-black absolute -bottom-2 -right-2"></div>

      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">Case Study</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black mt-2">Predirect</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mt-3">
        A one-install Manifest V3 extension that rewrites 30+ tracked sites
        (YouTube, X, Reddit, Google…) to privacy-friendly frontends. No
        settings, no thinking required.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-6">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/pritkr/predirect"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-[var(--yellow)] border-2 border-black text-black font-bold hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-transform shadow-[3px_3px_0_#000]"
        >
          <i class="ri-github-fill text-lg mr-2"></i>Repository
        </a>
        <a
          href="/posts/post-1"
          class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-[#BEE7FF] border-2 border-black text-black font-bold hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-transform shadow-[3px_3px_0_#000]"
        >
          <i class="ri-article-line text-lg mr-2"></i>Full story
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold">
        <a
          href="#redirect-playground"
          class="underline decoration-2 underline-offset-2 hover:bg-[var(--yellow)] px-1 transition-colors"
        >
          Try the interactive route preview ↓
        </a>
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-8 mt-12">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Problem</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Every time I opened YouTube, X, or Reddit in a normal browser, I was
            being profiled — cookies, trackers, fingerprinting — before I'd even
            scrolled. The usual answer, "just use a private frontend", means
            juggling five tools and remembering five different URLs. Privacy
            tooling shouldn't be homework.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">My contribution</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            I designed and built the entire extension solo: the redirect map
            that knows how each tracked site's URLs are shaped, the
            Manifest&nbsp;V3 packaging, and the Chrome/Firefox/Edge builds.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Technical approach</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            The hard part was the redirect map. Every site has its own URL
            quirks, and a naive <code class="bg-[#FFFDEB] border border-black px-1">replace("youtube.com", "invidious.example")</code> breaks
            half the URLs. The map has to handle watch IDs, shorts, embeds, and
            paths without breaking the content — so the extension had to
            understand what kind of URL it was looking at, not just string-swap
            domains.
          </p>
        </div>

        <PredirectDemo />

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            <strong>270★ on GitHub</strong> and a working install on Chrome,
            Firefox, and Edge. One install, and YouTube becomes Invidious, X
            becomes a lightweight client, Reddit becomes a readable
            alternative — automatically.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">After release</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            The project stays alive through public maintenance: users open
            issues when a site breaks or a frontend goes down, and those issues
            drive the fixes. The best privacy tool is the one you don't notice —
            so most of the work now is keeping it invisible.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t-2 border-black mt-12 pt-6 text-sm">
        <p>
          Want the longer version?{" "}
          <a
            href="/posts/post-1"
            class="font-semibold underline decoration-2 underline-offset-2 hover:bg-[var(--yellow)] px-0.5"
          >
            How Predirect became my most-starred project →
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CallToAction />
  <Footer />
</Layout>
